## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

1. **`parser`** · [ticket #4](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/4):
   the shared parser reads every date month first, and day-first tenants get the day and month
   swapped. Every report from a tenant on `booking-v2`. This is the bug the queued fix is for.
2. **`hint`** · [ticket #2](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2):
   the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants' people type
   month first, as told, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. Every report from a tenant on
   `booking-v3`, whatever channel the complaint came in by: the table above files only the `form`
   channel here. The parser fix does not touch it: the form's hint does.
3. **one-day move** · [ticket #5](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/5):
   the reports the desk read as a one-day move (the note under the table). A date converted
   between time zones, not a day/month swap; neither fix touches it.

## How the reports were split

1. One id, one report: rows the export repeats count once.
2. Every report takes its cause from its tenant: where they are and which booking form they run
   (the tenant directory, as exported), not from the intake tag, which is a guess from the
   reporter's browser, and not from the channel the complaint came in by.
3. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) goes to the one-day ticket, not
   to its tenant's cause. Each report is counted once.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why one ticket hid three

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Reports about
different bugs use the same words ("Date is wrong"), so they landed in one ticket. Its own
consequence says engineering merges separate tickets later; nobody splits merged ones. 0001 is
accepted, so it stays as it is: [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-merge-on-cause) replaces it.

